# Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) — Implementation Plan

## Overview

This plan outlines how to implement hardcoded role-based access in Lumad Lingua so that each user role sees a **different bottom navigation bar** and can only access **their permitted screens**.

---

## Roles & Screen Access

| Screen | Learner | Contributor | Validator | Educator | Admin |
|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
| Home (Dashboard) | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Archive Map | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Dictionary | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Learning Hub | ✅ | ✅ | — | ✅ | ✅ |
| Profile | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Contributor | — | ✅ | — | — | ✅ |
| Validator | — | — | ✅ | — | ✅ |
| Educator Dashboard | — | — | — | ✅ | ✅ |
| Admin Panel | — | — | — | — | ✅ |

## Bottom Nav Tabs Per Role

| Role | Tabs |
|---|---|
| **Learner** | Home · Map · Words · Learn · You |
| **Contributor** | Home · Map · Words · Add · You |
| **Validator** | Home · Map · Words · Check · You |
| **Educator** | Home · Map · Words · Teach · You |
| **Admin** | Home · Map · Words · Admin · You |

---

## Step-by-Step Implementation

### Step 1: Create a Role Provider

Create a new file `lib/providers/role_provider.dart` that holds the current user's role as an enum. Since we're hardcoding everything, this will default to `learner` and can be changed from the login screen or profile.

```dart
// lib/providers/role_provider.dart
import 'package:flutter_riverpod/flutter_riverpod.dart';

enum UserRole { learner, contributor, validator, educator, admin }

class RoleNotifier extends Notifier<UserRole> {
  @override
  UserRole build() => UserRole.learner;

  void setRole(UserRole role) => state = role;
}

final roleProvider = NotifierProvider<RoleNotifier, UserRole>(
  RoleNotifier.new,
);
```

### Step 2: Define Nav Config Per Role

Create a helper that maps each role to its navigation items and routes. This keeps the `MainLayout` clean.

```dart
// lib/config/role_nav_config.dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import '../providers/role_provider.dart';

class NavItem {
  final IconData icon;
  final String label;
  final String route;
  const NavItem(this.icon, this.label, this.route);
}

List<NavItem> getNavItemsForRole(UserRole role) {
  // Common tabs everyone gets
  const home = NavItem(Icons.home_rounded, 'HOME', '/');
  const map = NavItem(Icons.map_rounded, 'MAP', '/map');
  const words = NavItem(Icons.menu_book_rounded, 'WORDS', '/dictionary');
  const profile = NavItem(Icons.person_rounded, 'YOU', '/profile');

  switch (role) {
    case UserRole.learner:
      return [home, map, words, NavItem(Icons.school_rounded, 'LEARN', '/learning'), profile];
    case UserRole.contributor:
      return [home, map, words, NavItem(Icons.add_circle_rounded, 'ADD', '/contribute'), profile];
    case UserRole.validator:
      return [home, map, words, NavItem(Icons.verified_rounded, 'CHECK', '/validate'), profile];
    case UserRole.educator:
      return [home, map, words, NavItem(Icons.history_edu_rounded, 'TEACH', '/educator-dashboard'), profile];
    case UserRole.admin:
      return [home, map, words, NavItem(Icons.admin_panel_settings_rounded, 'ADMIN', '/admin'), profile];
  }
}
```

### Step 3: Update the Login Screen

Add role selection to the login page. When the user taps "Sign In", set the role in the provider before navigating.

```dart
// In login_screen.dart — add a role selector dropdown/chips
// On login:
ref.read(roleProvider.notifier).setRole(selectedRole);
context.go('/');
```

### Step 4: Refactor MainLayout

Replace the current hardcoded 9-tab `BottomNavigationBar` with a dynamic one driven by the role provider.

Key changes to [main_layout.dart](file:///c:/Users/Aspire-3/Desktop/Lumad%20Lingua%20Flutter/lib/screens/main_layout.dart):
- Read `roleProvider` to get the current role
- Call `getNavItemsForRole(role)` to get the nav items
- Build the `BottomNavigationBar` from that list
- Derive `currentIndex` by matching the current route against the nav items

### Step 5: Guard Routes (Optional but Recommended)

Add a redirect in GoRouter that checks the user's role. If a learner tries to navigate to `/admin`, redirect them back to `/`.

```dart
// In main.dart router config
redirect: (context, state) {
  final container = ProviderScope.containerOf(context);
  final role = container.read(roleProvider);
  final loc = state.uri.toString();
  
  // Block unauthorized routes
  if (loc.startsWith('/admin') && role != UserRole.admin) return '/';
  if (loc.startsWith('/validate') && role != UserRole.validator && role != UserRole.admin) return '/';
  if (loc.startsWith('/contribute') && role != UserRole.contributor && role != UserRole.admin) return '/';
  if (loc.startsWith('/educator') && role != UserRole.educator && role != UserRole.admin) return '/';
  
  return null; // Allow navigation
},
```

### Step 6: Conditionally Show Dashboard Sections

Some dashboard cards should only appear for certain roles (e.g., "Daily Rituals" for learners, "Pending Reviews" for validators). Use the role provider in the dashboard to conditionally render widgets.

---

## Implementation Order

| # | Task | File(s) |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Create `role_provider.dart` | `lib/providers/role_provider.dart` |
| 2 | Create `role_nav_config.dart` | `lib/config/role_nav_config.dart` |
| 3 | Add role selector to Login screen | `lib/screens/login_screen.dart` |
| 4 | Refactor `MainLayout` nav bar | `lib/screens/main_layout.dart` |
| 5 | Add route guards to GoRouter | `lib/main.dart` |
| 6 | Conditionally render dashboard sections | `lib/screens/dashboard_screen.dart` |

> [!TIP]
> Since you want everything hardcoded first, steps 1–4 are the most impactful. Steps 5–6 are polish that can come after.
